vo_avfoundation: prime the OSD layer before its first subtitle

An AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer that has never shown an image shows the first
sample it is handed at once, whatever its timestamp; every later sample
waits for its time on the layer's timebase. The OSD layer gets no sample
until the first subtitle (osd_layer_dirty keeps a subtitle-less layer
without an image), and flip_page enqueues that subtitle with its frame,
queue-lead-ms ahead. So the first subtitle a VO showed came a queue lead
early: a sign that starts on a cut sat over the last frames of the shot
before it (about 100 ms, 6 display frames at 60 Hz, in an iPhone screen
recording; 117 ms on the iPhone Air simulator). Later subtitles, and the
first after a seek of a layer that had shown one, were on time: the layer
had an image by then.

Before a subtitle goes to a layer that never had one, a transparent sample
marked to display at once goes first (as clear_osd_layer does after a
seek), so the subtitle is not the layer's first sample and waits for its
frame. A file without subtitles still never gives the layer an image. The
transparent sample is stamped with the layers' clock as it is, like
clear_osd_layer's, so it never comes after a stamp of 0050's.

iPhone Air simulator, iOS 27.0, an episode whose first subtitle is a sign
starting on a cut, the time the subtitle layer first shows the sign less
the time the video layer shows the cut, read every display refresh
(displayedPixelBuffer of both layers): opened at a point before the sign
-117 ms in each of 3 runs -> 0 ms in each of 4 (with and without 0050);
opened earlier, playing through other subtitles and seeking to the same
point: 0 ms before and after.

diff --git a/video/out/vo_avfoundation.m b/video/out/vo_avfoundation.m
index 5d666d2..f7b32f9 100644
--- a/video/out/vo_avfoundation.m
+++ b/video/out/vo_avfoundation.m
@@ -3727,6 +3727,31 @@ static int64_t layer_time_ns(struct priv *p)
     return p->timebase ? cm_time_to_ns(CMTimebaseGetTime(p->timebase)) : 0;
 }
 
+// A sample buffer layer that has never shown an image shows the first sample
+// it is handed at once, whatever its timestamp, while every later one waits
+// for its time on the layer's timebase. The OSD layer gets nothing until the
+// first subtitle (osd_layer_dirty), and that subtitle is enqueued a queue
+// lead (~120 ms) ahead of its frame, so it showed that much early: a sign
+// over the last frames of the shot before it. Hand such a layer a
+// transparent sample to show at once first; the subtitle then waits for its
+// frame. A layer that never shows a subtitle still never gets an image.
+static void prime_osd_layer(struct vo *vo)
+{
+    struct priv *p = vo->priv;
+
+    if (p->osd_layer_dirty || !p->osdLayer)
+        return;
+    CVPixelBufferRef pixbuf = create_empty_osd_pixel_buffer(vo);
+    if (!pixbuf)
+        return;
+    CMSampleBufferRef buf = create_image_sample_buffer(vo, pixbuf, layer_time_ns(p), true);
+    CVPixelBufferRelease(pixbuf);
+    if (!buf)
+        return;
+    enqueue_osd_sample(vo, buf);
+    CFRelease(buf);
+}
+
 // Make the OSD layer show nothing, dropping what is queued for it, without
 // removing its image. Removing the displayed image (flush with removal)
 // hands the layer's video receiver an empty configuration on every seek,
@@ -4068,6 +4093,8 @@ static void present_pending_osd(struct vo *vo, bool flush)
         CMSampleBufferRef buf = create_osd_sample_buffer(vo, e->pts_ns, &needed);
         if (buf) {
             bool has_subtitle = p->has_subtitle && p->cachedSubtitleBuffer;
+            if (has_subtitle)
+                prime_osd_layer(vo);
             int64_t t = mp_time_ns();
             bool enqueued = enqueue_osd_sample(vo, buf);
             p->perf.enqueue_ns += mp_time_ns() - t;
@@ -5362,6 +5389,8 @@ static void flip_page(struct vo *vo)
                 update_media_timebase_for_frame(vo);
 
             if (osd_buf) {
+                if (osd_buf_has_subtitle)
+                    prime_osd_layer(vo);
                 t = mp_time_ns();
                 osd_enqueued = enqueue_osd_sample(vo, osd_buf);
                 p->perf.enqueue_ns += mp_time_ns() - t;
